    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d644">

                <pb facs="0619" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/8: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-17T13:00:00+01:00">September 17,
                            1939—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 17—9:44 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2016. Waterman’s 13 of September 16, 10 a.m.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d644-f1"/>
                    regarding enemy aliens included in the crews of American ships. I have informed
                    Waterman as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Embassy has no intention of intervening in behalf of enemy aliens
                            included in the crews of American ships and the Department has been so
                            informed. I desire that you take no action in this respect without prior
                            consultation with the Embassy.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d644-f1" n="26" xml:id="d644-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; Henry S. Waterman, Consul at Bordeaux, had reported that French
                    authorities intended to remove enemy nationals from crews of American ships
                    (340.1115A/2).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
